{
 "@context": {
  "prov": "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#",
  "dct": "http://purl.org/dc/terms/",
  "dcat": "http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#",
  "rdfs": "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#",
  "cwp": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/pipeline#"
 },
 "@graph": [
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchwildlife",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "fetch-wildlife",
   "dct:description": "Fetches the open occurrence records of 21 species (20 urban and river birds, the red fox) in the model box from NBN Atlas and GBIF into data/raw/wildlife/ (fetch), then classifies each record located to 100 m or better by a 10 m habitat raster made from area.js water and the trees.json green areas, and writes counts per species, habitat class and month, flock sizes and blended habitat weights to docklands/data/wildlife.json (build; no network).",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcnbnatlas",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://records-ws.nbnatlas.org/occurrences/search",
     "dct:description": "q=*:*, wkt = the model box, fq=species:<name>, fq=license:(CC0 OR CC-BY OR OGL), 1,000 a page; fields lat, lon, uncertainty, month, year, resource, licence, count"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcgbif",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.gbif.org/v1/occurrence/search",
     "dct:description": "geometry = the model box, taxonKey (species/match), datasetKey = the three allowed, license = CC0_1_0 or CC_BY_4_0, 300 a page"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/area.js"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/trees.json"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/localdatarawwildlife"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/wildlife.json"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/fetch-wildlife.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/fetch-wildlife.mjs [fetch|build]",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Box: the model extent (area.js meta.extent) as a WGS84 polygon through the inverse of meta.geo.",
    "Licences: NBN Atlas records with record licence CC0, CC-BY or OGL, less the resources with a non-commercial resource licence (dr2992 Birda, dr671 National Mammal Atlas Project); GBIF records with licence CC0 or CC BY from iNaturalist research grade, NABU|naturgucker and TIPU only. eBird, every CC BY-NC record and GiGL are not used.",
    "Politeness: one request at a time, at least 1 s apart; retried with a doubling pause on 429 or 5xx.",
    "Habitat raster: water by the docklands/water.js rule (tidal = river; a dock or basin name, or 20,000 m2 and over below 6 m OD = dock; else pond); green kinds: wood (wood, forest, scrub, nature reserve, TOW small woodland and NFI) over park (parks, grass, pitches, recreation grounds, playing fields) over garden (gardens, allotments, churchyards, cemeteries); water over greens.",
    "A record of a waterbird within 30 m of water counts as that water (records made from the bank); other species: the class at the point.",
    "Weights: fewer than 10 located records: the ecology prior of the tool; else half the prior and half the record share (scaled to the prior maximum). Season: three-month smoothed monthly counts, scaled to a peak of 1, when 24 or more records are dated."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuilddocklands"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuildtrees"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "water",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "The ecology priors (relative weights per habitat), the season priors of the layer and the densities per habitat class (docklands/layers/wildlife.js DENS) are hand-entered from general knowledge of London birds; they are stated in the file and on the page."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfindkml",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "find-kml",
   "dct:description": "Answers the owner's question 'Can you find any kml resources for the area?' (2026-10-05). A hand list of candidates, found by searching the project's own catalogues (London Datastore resources with format kml/kmz, the raw data.gov.uk walk: 4,499 of 59,451 datasets have a KML resource) and the open-data hubs of TfL, Walk Wheel Cycle Trust and Canal & River Trust, is fetched as the 3D page would fetch it (Origin header of the Pages site) and read with the page's own reader docklands/kml.js (a DOMParser from @xmldom/xmldom, description HTML through linkedom). For each: HTTP status, https, the CORS header, the counts of placemarks in the zone and in the model box, unsupported elements. Open layers that cannot be opened by URL (no KML, or a whole-London file) are written as zone-clipped KML with the page's writer into cwplans/feeds/kml/, with the source, licence and attribution in the Document description. Result: feeds/kml/catalogue.json and README.md.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srckmlcatalogue"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srckmltflgishub"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srckmlsustransncn"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srckmlcrtlocks"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srclds2jx1l"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/portals/dgu/national-trails-england3/national-trails-england3.geojson"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/portals/pdg/listed-building/listed-building.geojson"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/portals/pdg/world-heritage-site/world-heritage-site.geojson"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/portals/pdg/world-heritage-site-buffer-zone/world-heritage-site-buffer-zone.geojson"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/portals/pdg/heritage-at-risk/heritage-at-risk.geojson"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/portals/pdg/park-and-garden/park-and-garden.geojson"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/london-datastore/conservation-areas/conservation-areas.geojson"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/kml.js"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/catalogue.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/tfl-cycle-routes.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/tfl-river-piers.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/tfl-river-services.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/sustrans-ncn.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/crt-locks.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/ne-thames-path.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/he-listed-buildings.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/he-world-heritage.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/he-heritage-at-risk.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/he-parks-gardens.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/gla-conservation-areas.kml"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/kml/lds-wards-2016-zone.kml"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/find-kml.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 KML_DOM_DIR=<dir with @xmldom/xmldom and linkedom> node cwplans/tools/find-kml.mjs <copy [id ...]|probe|all>",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Politeness: one request at a time, at least 1.1 s apart, robots.txt read per host with walk-portals.mjs allowed() and obeyed, the project User-Agent.",
    "Licence class as walk-portals.mjs licenceClass; only ogl, cc-by, odc-by and public-domain layers are copied or offered as examples; share-alike (except OSM content inside an open layer, marked odbl and osm derived), restricted and no-licence resources are listed with the reason.",
    "cors yes = HTTP 200 over https and Access-Control-Allow-Origin * or https://danbri.github.io; a ?kml= link is made only for a file the reader parsed with at least one placemark in the zone.",
    "Zone = the model box plus the Royal Docks and the Thames Barrier, WGS84 -0.095, 51.47, 0.08, 51.53; copies keep features that meet the box (polygons whole, lines cut at the box edge with one vertex beyond), the names and a few fields.",
    "The copies are pushed to danbri/londat before the probe, which then reads them from raw.githubusercontent.com; the headless page test of every ?kml= link is stored in the catalogue as page_test."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolwalkportals"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "feeds",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "The candidate list, the fields kept in each copy and the colours are chosen by hand in the tool; the reasons for each listed (not usable) resource are in the tool and in feeds/kml/README.md."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchworks",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "fetch-works",
   "dct:description": "Fetches public permits, works, closures, planned events and markets for the Docklands zone (the 3D model box plus the Royal Docks margin) from TfL, DfT Street Manager, The Gazette, Tower Hamlets, the Planning London Datahub and OSM, and harvests venue and council event programmes from the event feeds in feeds/events.json; writes one dated snapshot per source ({meta, items}) and works.json, every item in one normalised shape, for feeds/whatson.html.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/area.js"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srctflunifiedapi",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.tfl.gov.uk/Line/{ids}/Status/{from}/to/{to}?detail=true",
     "dct:description": "every line of modes tube, dlr, elizabeth-line, overground, river-bus, cable-car (Line/Mode/...) plus c2c, southeastern, southern, thameslink, greater-anglia; 12 ids per request; from = fetch date 00:00, to = +90 days"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srctflunifiedapi",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.tfl.gov.uk/Line/Mode/bus/Status?detail=true",
     "dct:description": "all bus routes with disruptions (13 MB)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srctflunifiedapi",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.tfl.gov.uk/StopPoint/Mode/bus/Disruption?includeRouteBlockedStops=true",
     "dct:description": "all bus stop disruptions"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srctflunifiedapi",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.tfl.gov.uk/Road/all/Disruption and /Road/all/Street/Disruption",
     "dct:description": "stripContent=true, startDate = fetch date, endDate = +90 days"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcnaptan",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://naptan.api.dft.gov.uk/v1/access-nodes",
     "dct:description": "atcoAreaCodes=490 (bus) and 910,930,940 (stations), dataFormat=csv; cached"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcdftstreetmanager",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://opendata.manage-roadworks.service.gov.uk/{permit,activity}/YYYY/MM.zip",
     "dct:description": "the last full month (default); about 1 GB and 13 MB; cached"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcthegazette",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://www.thegazette.co.uk/all-notices/notice/data.json and https://www.thegazette.co.uk/notice/{id}",
     "dct:description": "noticetypes 1501 and 1503 x text = each zone authority, start-publish-date = fetch date - 120 days, 100 per page; then each notice page (cached)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcthlicensingnotices",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://www.towerhamlets.gov.uk/lgnl/business/licences/alcohol_and_entertainment/Licence_applications_received_this_week.aspx and .../markets/markets_in_tower_hamlets.aspx",
     "dct:description": "HTML GET"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcpostcodesio",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.postcodes.io/postcodes",
     "dct:description": "bulk POST, 100 postcodes per request"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcplanninglondondatahub",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://planningdata.london.gov.uk/api-guest/applications/_search",
     "dct:description": "POST Elasticsearch query: \"temporary\" + an event word + geo_bounding_box of the zone, 300 newest by last_updated"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/events.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcvenueeventfeeds",
     "dcat:accessURL": "the feed URL of every verified event feed in feeds/events.json, read at run time",
     "dct:description": "HTTP GET (POST with the entry request_body when it has one); ICS, RSS/Atom or WordPress REST JSON"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcosm",
     "dcat:accessURL": "data/raw/docklands/greater_london-latest.osm.pbf (local)",
     "dct:description": "amenity=marketplace nodes and ways; named highways for council-page markets"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/tfl-lines.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/tfl-bus.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/tfl-road.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/street-manager.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/street-manager-activities.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/gazette.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/th-licences.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/planning.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/markets.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/venue-events.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/works/works.json"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/fetch-works.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/fetch-works.mjs [tfl-lines tfl-bus tfl-road street-manager gazette th-licences planning markets venue-events] [--no-fetch] [--refresh] [--days=90] [--month=YYYY-MM]",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Zone: \"model\" = WGS84 -0.095, 51.474 to 0.015, 51.522 (BOX_WGS84 of fetch-docklands.mjs; the tool prints the BNG box from docklands/data/area.js meta.extent: E 532400-539900, N 176700-182300); \"east\" = 0.015, 51.495 to 0.085, 51.522 (Royal Docks, ExCeL, City Airport). Items outside both are dropped and counted.",
    "TfL lines: a status is kept when an affected stop lies in the zone; TfL sends lat/lon 0, so stops are placed through NaPTAN (stop-area id 940G/910G/930G -> station entry 9400/9100/9300, else by station name); a status naming no stops is kept only for a line that serves the zone (line-wide). Validity periods kept; start = first from, end = last to.",
    "TfL buses: route disruptions grouped by identical text; kept when the text names a stop that lies in the zone on one of its routes, else when its opening \"STREET, DISTRICT:\" is a district wholly in the zone (E1, E1W, E14, E16, EC3*, SE8, SE10, SE16); a borough name alone does not place a diversion. Stop closures placed by the NaPTAN position of their ATCO code, grouped by text and dates.",
    "TfL roads: disruptions active in the 90-day window whose TfL point lies in the zone; closed street segments of the same disruption id attached (at most 12).",
    "Street Manager: unzip -p of the monthly archive split on }{\"event_reference\": (record count must equal the zip file count); BNG prefilter on the first coordinate, then OSTN15 to WGS84 and the zone test; the latest event per permit or activity reference. Permits kept when not cancelled, refused, revoked or closed and the end (actual, else proposed) is on or after the fetch date. Activities: skips and scaffolding counted, not kept; cancelled and ended dropped.",
    "Gazette: robots.txt Crawl-delay 10 s between requests; only data.json searches and /notice/{id} pages (data.jsonld/.ttl/.rdf/.xml and ?view=linked-data are disallowed). The search geo point is the publisher office, so a notice is kept by issuing authority (zone councils, or Transport for London naming a zone borough). TTRO = text says temporary, section 14, 16A or experimental. Dates = day-month-year phrases on or after publication. Submitter (f:name, f:familyName) and signatory names dropped.",
    "Tower Hamlets licences: the weekly table; premises-name column dropped (it sometimes holds a private licence holder name); placed at the postcode centre (postcodes.io, ONSPD). One week per snapshot; history is the git history of the snapshot.",
    "Planning London Datahub: description has \"temporary\" and an event word (event, marquee, festival, stage, market, fair, funfair, ice rink, pop-up, filming, concert, exhibition); centroid in the zone; applications validated more than two years before the fetch dropped; description cut to 220 characters; facts and link only (GLA terms not confirmed as OGL).",
    "Markets: OSM amenity=marketplace in the zone from the local extract (ways at the mean of their nodes); Tower Hamlets markets page parsed for name, days, place and times and joined by name, else placed on the OSM street it names.",
    "Venue events: the feeds are read from feeds/events.json at run time (category ical, rss-atom, rest-api or whats-on-page; verified; a feed URL; ics, rss, atom or json; id, name or subject about events or what is on; not news, press releases, consultations, meetings, warnings, closures, works or notices; harvest: true/false on an entry overrides), so feeds added there join automatically. Kept per event: title (cut to 160), dates, venue, position, link; no description text. Date from the feed event fields (ICS DTSTART, RSS ev:startdate, WordPress ACF dates), a date in the title or link, or the Atom published day where checked by hand (Royal Docks, midnight entries only); events from today to 180 days ahead; undated items only from single-venue programmes. Position: postcode in the item, else the venue of the feed host (VENUES table, through its postcode). The Royal Docks feed mixes articles with events: only /whats-on/ links.",
    "Gazette office postcodes (SE18 6HQ, SE6 4RU, E16 2QU, SE1 2QH, SE1 8NJ, SE1P 5LX, EC2V 7HH, EC2P 2EJ, E1 0HJ, E1 1BJ) are removed before postcode districts are read.",
    "Network: User-Agent glitchcan-cwplans/0.1; one request at a time per host, at least 1 s apart (10 s for www.thegazette.co.uk); up to 5 tries with Retry-After or a doubling pause on 429, 5xx, timeouts and resets. Raw responses in data/raw/works/ (gitignored); NaPTAN, Street Manager archives and Gazette notice pages reused unless --refresh; --no-fetch rebuilds from the raw files."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "feeds",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "Zone margins, the rail lines treated as serving the zone, the postcode districts treated as wholly in the zone, the event words of the planning query and the dropped fields (premises names, submitter names, skips and scaffolding) are choices recorded in skills/cwplans-permits-and-works/SKILL.md and feeds/works/README.md."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchrawgrid",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "fetch-raw-grid",
   "dct:description": "Downloads the OSTN15 grid that every WGS84 to British National Grid conversion in the project uses (tools/lib.mjs bngProjector).",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcosostn15",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://cdn.proj.org/uk_os_OSTN15_NTv2_OSGBtoETRS.tif",
     "dct:description": "the OS OSTN15 NTv2 transformation grid (GeoTIFF) as distributed by the PROJ CDN"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/localdatarawukosostn15ntv2osgbtoetrstif"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/fetch-raw.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "node cwplans/tools/fetch-raw.mjs grid",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "The file is written as fetched; no change.",
    "Network: one GET with User-Agent glitchcan-cwplans/0.1; no retry; the file is overwritten on every run (no cache)."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "terrain",
   "cwp:fault": []
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchrawosm",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "fetch-raw-osm",
   "dct:description": "Fetches the OSM map call for the small corridor box, then the full geometry of water multipolygons whose member ways the map call leaves out (the Pool of London).",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcosm",
