   "cwp:command": "node cwplans/tools/build-splats.mjs [--ground 4] [--cell 7.2] [--box x0,x1,z0,z1]",
   "cwp:kind": "derive",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Box: the model's focus box plus 300 m unless --box is given.",
    "Ground discs every 4 m (--ground) where no building covers the cell, coloured bilinearly from rgb2008.ppm.",
    "Roof discs every 4 m inside the outline: aerial colour on buildings under 40 m, else the building colour.",
    "Walls: one disc per 3.6 m storey and 7.2 m (--cell) of wall, and one glass-band disc 3 cm in front per cell (buildings 4 m or taller).",
    "The set entry 'cw-synth' replaces any earlier one in index.json; other entries are kept.",
    "every splat records its building (uint16 index into cw-synth.json groups; 65535 = ground) for animation",
    "Positions in model metres (x east, y up, z south); 32-byte .splat records, gzipped."
   ],
   "cwp:network": false,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuilddocklands"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuildaerialrgb2008"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "splats",
   "cwp:fault": []
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuildriver",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "build-river",
   "dct:description": "Rasterises the Thames water polygons on an 8 m grid and finds the centreline from the west to the east edge of the model by a least-cost path that keeps away from the banks; also copies the Eden Dock outline.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/area.js"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/river.json"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/build-river.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "node cwplans/tools/build-river.mjs",
   "cwp:kind": "derive",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "the Thames = tidal water polygons with no name (or named Thames)",
    "step cost = step length / (distance to bank + 1)^1.5",
    "moving average over 9 cells, resampled every 20 m",
    "Start and end: the widest water cell (largest distance to the bank) in the westmost and eastmost grid columns that hold water.",
    "Rounding: points and half-widths to 0.1 m; Eden Dock ring to 0.1 m."
   ],
   "cwp:network": false,
   "cwp:deterministic": true,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuilddocklands"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "water",
   "cwp:fault": []
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuildpiers",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "build-piers",
   "dct:description": "Piers, pontoons and berthed vessels in the 3D model box for the Three.js port's piers layer. Reads the OSM pier shapes (man_made=pier ways and multipolygons, with inner rings) and ship outlines (building=ship, historic=ship) from the local Greater London extract; a fixed pier keeps its outline, with its deck at the highest land under it; a floating pier is rasterised at 0.5 m and cut by local width into pontoons (oriented rectangles) and gangways or walks (shore end and the height of the land there). Joins the TfL river-bus piers of feeds/river/river-bus.json with the lines TfL lists at each pier (one StopPoint request; offline: the held route sequences), the tour-boat facts read from two operators' pages (City Cruises, Thames River Sightseeing; held in the tool with URL and date), and Wikidata items of feeds/river/wikidata-vessels.json; finds the berth beside each passenger pier's largest pontoon, and for each ship outline its length, beam, heading (bow = the narrower end) and the model buildings it replaces.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/localdatarawdocklandsgreaterlondonlatestosmpbf"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srctflunifiedapi",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.tfl.gov.uk/StopPoint/Mode/river-bus",
     "dct:description": "one GET: the lines at each river-bus pier (skipped with --offline)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/area.js"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/river.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/river/river-bus.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/river/wikidata-vessels.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srctouroperatorpages"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/piers.json"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/build-piers.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/build-piers.mjs [--offline]",
   "cwp:kind": "derive",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Floating: floating=yes, or a name with Pier or Pontoon and no floating=no; a name with Jetty or ending in Wharf (and no Pier) is fixed.",
    "Cut: a part is wide when it is within T of a cell at least T from the outside (an opening); T = 0.62 x the largest half-width, at least 2.2 m and at most 4.5 m, raised 0.4 m at a time (to 0.9 x) while a wide part fills under 60 % of its rectangle; wide parts of 40 m2 or more are pontoons; a narrow part at least 5.5 m wide and 15 m long is a pontoon unless it touches a pontoon and is 3.5 times as long as wide (then an access bridge, drawn as a gangway up to 6 m wide).",
    "TfL pier join: the named floating OSM pier with the largest pontoon within 80 m of the TfL position; no shape (Doubletree Docklands / Nelson Dock Pier): a 30 x 7 m pontoon 18 m from the bank with a gangway (stated default).",
    "Berth: the long side of the largest pontoon nearer the Thames centreline (docklands/data/river.json); bow upstream = towards the lower centreline index.",
    "Heights: land = the terrain of area.js where the point is not in a water polygon; default 5.3 m OD on the Thames (river wall) and 1 m above a dock.",
    "Ships: only outlines in water polygons (Cutty Sark, in dry dock, stays a building); hidden model buildings = those whose outline centre is inside the ship's rectangle plus 1 m.",
    "Rounding: 0.1 m, angles 0.001 rad. The OSM read is cached in the system temp folder by extract size and time; the output is the same from run to run when the inputs and the TfL lines are the same."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuilddocklands"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuildriver"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchriver"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "water",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "The tour-boat facts (piers, frequencies, first and last departures by season) and the stated defaults (Thames River Sightseeing frequency, the synthetic pontoon, the heights) are hand-entered in the tool, with the page and date in docklands/data/piers.json meta.tours."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfittideharmonics",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "fit-tide-harmonics",
   "dct:description": "Fits a mean and tidal harmonic constituents by least squares to the Environment Agency 15-minute tidal levels of the three gauges round the 3D model, so that the 3D pages can show the tide at any time (the EA publishes readings, not predictions; PLA and UKHO predictions are not open). Two stages: a fetch stage (network, cached) and a fit stage that reads only the cached files.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srceafloodmonitoring",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://environment.data.gov.uk/flood-monitoring/id/measures/{station}-level-tidal_level-i-15_min-mAOD/readings",
     "dct:description": "stations 0007 Tower Pier, 0003 Charlton, 0001 Silvertown; startdate=today-45 days, enddate=today, _sorted, _limit=10000 (the API keeps about four weeks); plus /id/stations/{station} for the position"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srceafloodmonitoring",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://environment.data.gov.uk/flood-monitoring/archive/readings-{YYYY-MM-DD}.csv",
     "dct:description": "one daily archive file (all stations, about 60 MB) every 7 days from 10 to 371 days back, streamed; only the lines of the three tidal-level measures are kept"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/localdatarawrivertideapidatejsondatarawrivertidearchivedatecsvthecachedreadingstheirsha256iswrittenintotheoutput"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/tide-harmonics.json"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/fit-tide-harmonics.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/fit-tide-harmonics.mjs [--archive-days 371] [--archive-step 7] [--no-fetch]",
   "cwp:kind": "derive",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Readings: the API readings (about four weeks) and one archive day in seven back to a year (no archive file for some days: skipped); one request at a time; three retries 3, 6 and 9 s apart on timeouts and 5xx; User-Agent glitchcan-cwplans/0.1; cached files are not fetched again.",
    "Cleaning: a reading is dropped when its difference from the nearest other gauge departs more than 0.45 m from the median of that difference over 2 h either side (docklands/sky.js cleanGauges, fault F21); after a first fit, readings with a residual over 1.2 m are dropped (gauge faults and the largest surges).",
    "Constituents, in priority order M2, S2, N2, K1, O1, M4, MS4, MN4, M6, K2, P1, L2, NU2, MU2, 2N2, Q1, MK4, S4, 2MS6, 2MN6, M3, MK3, MO3, J1, OO1, M8, 3MS8, 2SM6, T2, MSf, Mf, Mm, Ssa, Sa; one is kept only when its speed differs from every kept one by at least 360 degrees over the span of the readings (Rayleigh criterion 1).",
    "Arguments: mean longitudes of the Moon, Sun, lunar perigee, node and solar perigee (Meeus), tau = 15 deg/h x UT + h - s; nodal factors f and u by the formulas of Pugh (1987, table 4.3); compound tides from their parts; L2 takes the M2 factors (a simplification). Phases are lags on these arguments, not Admiralty phases. The code is docklands/tide.js, which the 3D page uses too.",
    "Validation: a fit without 3 and 4 October 2026 (UTC) and the last 48 h of readings is compared with them (rms, maximum, high and low water height and time); the constituents written use all readings. Units m AOD, phases in degrees, amplitudes to 0.1 mm.",
    "Output also holds the cleaned readings of the last 7 days (15-minute slots, null where none), so the page shows a measured level where it has one, and check values (predictions every 6 h on 10 October 2026) that the page compares with its own prediction."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "sky",
   "cwp:fault": [
    "F21"
   ],
   "cwp:judgement": "The choice of constituents, the cleaning thresholds and the one-day-in-seven archive sampling are stated defaults (this activity's rules); the foreshore profiles drawn from the prediction are defaults in docklands/layers/tide.js."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchsky",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "fetch-sky",
   "dct:description": "Fetches the star catalogue, the constellation lines, satellite orbital elements, hourly weather and tide-gauge readings for the Sky panel of the 3D page (docklands/sky.js) and writes small JSON snapshots; the weather and tide files cover the London date given and the next day (the owner's photo evening, 3 October 2026).",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcyalebsc5",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/ftp/V/50/catalog.gz",
     "dct:description": "the whole catalogue, fixed-width text (gzip)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcd3celestial",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ofrohn/d3-celestial/master/data/constellations.lines.json",
     "dct:description": "GeoJSON MultiLineString per constellation"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srccelestrak",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://celestrak.org/NORAD/elements/gp.php",
     "dct:description": "CATNR=25544 (ISS), CATNR=48274 (Tiangong), GROUP=visual; FORMAT=json (OMM)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcopenmeteo",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast",
     "dct:description": "latitude=51.505, longitude=-0.02, start_date=DATE, end_date=DATE+1, hourly cloud cover (total, low, mid, high), visibility, humidity, dew point, precipitation, weather code, temperature, wind; timezone Europe/London; model best_match"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srceafloodmonitoring",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://environment.data.gov.uk/flood-monitoring/id/measures/{station}-level-tidal_level-i-15_min-mAOD/readings",
     "dct:description": "stations 0007 Tower Pier, 0003 Charlton, 0001 Silvertown; startdate=DATE, enddate=DATE+2, _sorted, _limit=1000; plus /id/stations/{station} for the position"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srciauwgsn",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://www.pas.rochester.edu/~emamajek/WGSN/IAU-CSN.txt",
     "dct:description": "the whole IAU Catalog of Star Names, fixed-column text (UTF-8)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcheasarcmessier",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/db-perl/W3Browse/w3query.pl",
     "dct:description": "tablehead=name=heasarc_messier, Action=Query, ResultMax=0, displaymode=BatchDisplay, Fields=All, Coordinates=Equatorial, Equinox=2000 (pipe-separated text)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srceumetsatclm",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://view.eumetsat.int/geoserver/wms",
     "dct:description": "WMS 1.3.0 GetMap, layers=msg_fes:clm, crs=EPSG:4326, bbox=50.5,-1.6,52.5,1.6, 256 x 256, image/png, time=the 15-minute slot (default DATE 23:00Z)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcosm",
     "dcat:accessURL": "data/raw/docklands/greater_london-latest.osm.pbf (local, extract osmfr-greater-london)",
     "dct:description": "osmium extract -b 0.03,51.495,0.08,51.51, tags-filter w/aeroway=runway, export geojson; the way with ref 09/27"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/stars.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/constellation-lines.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/sats-2026-10-03.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/weather-2026-10-03.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/tide-2026-10-03.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/star-names.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/messier.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/clm-20261003T2300Z.png"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/sky/lcy-approach.json"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/fetch-sky.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/fetch-sky.mjs [stars] [lines] [sats] [weather] [tide] [names] [messier] [clouds [2026-10-03T23:00Z]] [lcy] [--date 2026-10-03]",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Stars: Bright Star Catalogue rows with a J2000 position and V <= 5.5 (2,887); columns from the CDS ReadMe: HR 1-4, RA 76-83, Dec 84-90, Vmag 103-107, B-V 110-114; RA and Dec to 0.001 degree, V and B-V to 0.01; a missing B-V becomes 0.6; sorted by V.",
    "Constellation lines: every line string kept; longitude turned into RA 0-360 degrees; coordinates rounded to 0.01 degree. The Milky Way outlines of the same repository are not fetched (no stated licence); the page computes the band from galactic coordinates.",
    "Satellites: the three requests merged, one record per NORAD catalogue number; OMM fields kept as published. CelesTrak keeps no history, so a snapshot holds the elements current at fetch time (run within a day or two of the date). One request per group per run (CelesTrak: at most one download per 2 hours).",
    "Weather: the forecast API's past hours (best_match model, UK Met Office UKV first for London; it has visibility, which the ERA5 archive lacks); values as published, hourly, London time.",
    "Tide: 15-minute instantaneous readings in m AOD, UTC times, sorted; no gap filling; EA gives readings only, no predictions. The page (sky.js cleanGauges) leaves out a reading whose difference from the nearest other gauge departs more than 0.45 m from the median of that difference over 2 h either side (fault F21), then interpolates linearly by chainage along data/river.json between the gauges. The EA has no tidal gauge between Tower Pier and Charlton (station search of 2026-10-04, 15 km round the estate).",
    "Star names: rows of IAU-CSN whose designation is an HR number present in stars.json (324 of 451 names); columns found by the positions of the header titles (Name/Diacritics, Designation, Con), because names can hold spaces; the diacritic form is kept.",
    "Clouds: the EUMETSAT cloud mask PNG kept as sent. The page (sky.js) reads white pixels (R, G, B > 200) as cloud, takes the mean over 60 km round the box centre, and raises each layer's Open-Meteo cover by 0.9 x (local mask - mean), clamped to 0..1, so the mask places the cloud and Open-Meteo keeps the amount; the mask moves with 2.2 x the 10 m wind for up to 90 minutes from its slot. Other times only with Fetch ticked (EUMETView sends CORS headers; the mask appears about 25 minutes after the slot; none before 2020-09-01). Parallax (about 1.6 km north for cloud at 1 km over London) is not corrected.",
    "London City Airport: the landing thresholds are the two ends of the main runway way (ref 09/27; its displaced-threshold ways are left out); the page draws each approach as the extended centreline rising at 5.5 degrees (the published glide path) from 15 m over the threshold (50 ft assumed) out to 12 km. No live aircraft: OpenSky (written licence for any live product), adsb.fi (personal non-commercial), ADS-B Exchange (commercial), adsb.lol (ODbL share-alike) and airplanes.live (terms behind a bot challenge) were checked on 2026-10-04.",
    "Messier: all 109 rows of the HEASARC table (M 102 is not in it); RA and Dec from sexagesimal J2000 to degrees (0.001); size = the larger dimension in arcmin; the notes column title-cased as the common name. OpenNGC was not used (CC BY-SA).",
    "Network: User-Agent glitchcan-cwplans/0.1; three retries 3, 6 and 9 s apart on timeouts and 5xx (the agent proxy drops connections now and then); 4xx is not retried; files overwritten on every run."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "sky",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "Source choice and licence decisions (BSC5 as public domain, d3-celestial lines as BSD-3, CelesTrak with no stated licence and flagged for review, Vieira Milky Way outlines refused) are recorded in data-register.json sources and docklands/README.md \"Sky, time, weather and tide\"."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolwalklondondatastore",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "walk-london-datastore",
   "dct:description": "Walks the London Datastore (a DataPress site with a CKAN-compatible API): reads the whole catalogue from the v3 export, writes it compact (one dataset per line); triages every dataset by written rules (licence class, relevance to the zone, kind, whether the project already holds or lists it, value themes, join keys, sensitivity, score); harvests the shortlisted open datasets and keeps the features that meet the 3D model box, as GeoJSON in WGS84 with a meta member (source, URLs, fetch date, licence, attribution, method, counts).",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcldscatalogue",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/api/v3/datasets/export.json",
     "dct:description": "GET, every public dataset in one response (11 MB on 2026-10-04)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcldscatalogue",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/api/action/package_search",
     "dct:description": "GET, no parameters (q, rows and start are ignored): all datasets with the CKAN organisation and maintainer"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcldscatalogue",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/api/v3/dataset/<id>",
     "dct:description": "only with --details: one GET per dataset (186 of 1,305 fetched on 2026-10-04; they added only a generic format and no archivedAt)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srclds23n41",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/download/23n41/<resource id>/<file>",
     "dct:description": "harvest air-quality-monitoring-sites: the resource named in HARVEST (GET)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srclds2gy3r",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/download/2gy3r/<resource id>/<file>",
     "dct:description": "harvest article4-office-residential: the resource named in HARVEST (GET)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srclds2og9g",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/download/2og9g/<resource id>/<file>",
     "dct:description": "harvest brownfield-register: the resource named in HARVEST (GET)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srclds23jxk",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/download/23jxk/<resource id>/<file>",
     "dct:description": "harvest central-activities-zone: the resource named in HARVEST (GET)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcldsemqwg",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/download/emqwg/<resource id>/<file>",
     "dct:description": "harvest conservation-areas: the resource named in HARVEST (GET)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srclds23697",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/download/23697/<resource id>/<file>",
     "dct:description": "harvest cultural-infrastructure: the resource named in HARVEST (GET)"
    },
