  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolcontribphotos",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "contrib-photos",
   "dct:description": "Operation rectify-facade-patches: for each facade region in photos.json, facade.py rectifies it (LSD segments, RANSAC vanishing points, homography) and measure.py cuts the measuring box and gives bay and floor periods (autocorrelation) and three colours (k-means in Lab); the patch is written to rect/<id>.jpg. Operation lift-contrib-photos: photos.json (identifications with evidence and confidence, judged facade notes, model heights) and the patch graph give a schema.org Photograph per photo and a node per building. Both graphs are named in kgx/external-heads.json. Operation cut-facade-tiles: the photos.json tiles (a cut of a rectified patch, a mirrored half for a symmetric face, or a vector pattern in metres with judged colours) -> 256 px PNG tiles (and SVG for a pattern) in tiles/ and the graph facade-tiles-<set>.",
