   "dct:description": "Operation key-model-buildings: every OSM building and building:part outline of the clip is put through the build's own steps (build-docklands.mjs polysOf, toRings with the focus-box tolerance, poly) and its encoded outline compared with the model's; the build's order (outlines without parts, then parts) aligns the model list with the OSM elements, so equal outlines (a multipolygon's outer that is also a building way) get the right element. Tags come from the full extract (osmium getid; the clip keeps no addresses). The graph holds, per OSM element, its OSM page, model indices, parent building of a part, registry link from the atlas, and the OSM name, house name, address, postcode, building type other than yes, levels and Wikidata item. building-keys.json is its projection for the page, with the SHA-256 of area.js and a fingerprint the page checks.",
