    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/fetch-river.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/fetch-river.mjs [pla-notices crt-notices thames-barrier levels osm-river locks eden-dock royal-docks ea-sondes ea-wims river-bus pla-moorings wikidata-vessels] [--no-fetch] [--list]",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Zone: model box -0.095,51.474 to 0.015,51.522; east margin 0.015,51.495 to 0.085,51.522 (as fetch-works); Lea strip -0.025,51.522 to 0.010,51.528. Server queries use the envelope -0.095,51.474 to 0.085,51.528; items are kept when their point (or one point) falls in the zone.",
    "Politeness: one request at a time per host, at least 1.1 s apart (3 s for web.archive.org), up to 5 tries with Retry-After or a doubling pause on 429, 5xx, timeouts and resets; 4xx not retried; User-Agent from tools/lib.mjs. QLever through lib.mjs qlever().",
    "PLA (licence not stated) and CRT (no open licence): facts and links only. PLA: the notice number from the link (the name field holds placeholders), kind by title keywords, centroid = mean of polygon vertices, bbox, 'portwide' when the bbox is wider than 0.3 degrees; notice text, polygons, comments, invoice references and staff names dropped. PLA moorings: contact numbers and e-mails dropped.",
    "CRT notices: type, reason and programme ids mapped with the lookups embedded in the notices page on 2026-10-04.",
    "Thames Barrier: rows of the planned-tests table; London local times converted to ISO with the day's BST/GMT offset.",
    "Levels: measures with no readings dropped; series that publish about once a minute (DIFF_*) thinned to the first reading per 15-minute slot plus the latest; no cleaning (Tower Pier low-water fault F21 left for the consumer).",
    "Locks: rules hand-written in feeds/river/locks-facts.json; position = centroid of the named OSM element; CRT notices matched by keywords in crt_match against title and waterway; every cited page re-checked by HTTP GET. Conflicting operator statements kept in 'conflicts'.",
    "Eden Dock: rows of the table wq-readings-table; temperature from the weather-item-value before 'Water Temperature', stamped with the fetch time. Position: OSM relation 18985240.",
    "Royal Docks: pdftotext -layout for per-sample values, -raw for cyanobacteria rows (colonies/ml and the result kept as printed); 'Royal George V Dock' mapped to King George V Dock (written form kept); positions = mean of the vertices in the west or east fifth of the OSM dock polygon, marked approximate.",
    "EA sondes: plausibility rules flag (never change) pH outside 6 to 9.5, negative turbidity or oxygen, ammonium over 50 mg/L (fault F24).",
    "EA WIMS: BNG to WGS84 by a Helmert transform (proj4, about 5 m); water points get their latest sample from the last 60 observations.",
    "TfL: longest stop sequence per line and direction; timetable from the first zone pier; arrivals kept at zone piers only.",
    "OSM: osmium extract of the envelope, tags-filter, export geojsonseq; deduplicated by type/id; unnamed seamarks and untyped elements counted, not listed.",
    "Raw responses cached under data/raw/river/<source>/ (gitignored); URLs that carry the run's date are cached under a stable key so --no-fetch works; snapshots overwritten on each run (git keeps history)."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "water",
   "cwp:fault": [
    "F21",
    "F24"
   ],
   "cwp:judgement": "Licence classes per source (facts only for PLA, CRT and the operators' pages); the lock rules in feeds/river/locks-facts.json are read and paraphrased by hand (recorded with URL and date); the sonde plausibility thresholds; the choice of stations and sondes. Recorded in skills/cwplans-river-and-water/SKILL.md and feeds/river/README.md."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolsolvephotosun",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "solve-photo-sun",
   "dct:description": "Solves a daytime photo's camera and capture time: a pinhole camera fitted to tower tops of the model, shadows on a level deck back-projected through it, and the sun azimuth matched to a time with astronomy-engine. Prints JSON; the results are copied by hand into the photo folder's README and the docklands-sky skill.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/reference/day-2026-10-04/points.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/towers.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/vendor/astronomy.browser.min.js"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/solve-photo-sun.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "node cwplans/tools/solve-photo-sun.mjs [docklands/reference/day-2026-10-04/points.json]",
   "cwp:kind": "derive",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Camera: heading (from grid north), tilt, roll and focal length by Nelder-Mead least squares on the landmark pixels; principal point fixed at the image centre; landmark = the apex (pyramid) or the centroid of the top tier at its top height in docklands/data/towers.json; a landmark with a null y is fitted in x only.",
    "Shadow: the pixel of a post foot and of the shadow of its cap are back-projected to the plane 1.5 m below the eye; sun grid azimuth = bearing foot->shadow + 180 degrees; true azimuth = grid + grid_to_true_deg (1.54 here). The azimuth does not depend on the assumed camera height; the printed shadow lengths do (given for 1.3, 1.5, 1.7 m).",
    "Time: astronomy-engine Equator(of date, aberration) + Horizon(refraction \"normal\") for the observer in the points file; bisection on the azimuth between 06:00 and 18:00 UTC of the date. Result = the time of the mean azimuth; range = the times of the smallest and largest azimuth.",
    "The library is run in a vm context; times are passed as that realm's Date (its instanceof check fails on a Date of the main realm).",
    "The 3D page view ?view=greenlandday uses the same four landmarks refitted with roll 0 (the page camera has no roll): heading 51.9, tilt 6.45, field 99.9, rms 2.7 px (fitted by a grid search in the session, numbers in the docklands-3d-page skill)."
   ],
   "cwp:network": false,
   "cwp:deterministic": true,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuildtowers"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "sky",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "The pixel positions in points.json are read by eye from 2x and 4x enlargements (which point is the foot of a post is a judgement: the base plate hides it); recorded in points.json and the README."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolsolvephotoview",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "solve-photo-view",
   "dct:description": "Solves the camera of any photo of the zone, ground or air: a pinhole camera with eye position, heading, pitch, roll, focal length and optional radial distortion k1, fitted by Levenberg-Marquardt (numeric Jacobian) to landmark pixels (tower tops, named places, given coordinates), shoreline pixels (distance to the projected OSM water outline) and horizon pixels (the sea-level dip from the eye height). Reports rms, formal 1-sigma per parameter from the covariance, per-point residuals and hold-out residuals. Library tools/view-mcp/view-lib.mjs, also served as the docklands-view MCP (tools/view-mcp/server.mjs).",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/reference/plane-2026-10/points.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/towers.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/area.js"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/reference/plane-2026-10/solution.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/reference/plane-2026-10/compare-photo-render.jpg"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/../tools/view-mcp/solve.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "node tools/view-mcp/solve.mjs cwplans/docklands/reference/plane-2026-10/points.json [--k1] --out cwplans/docklands/reference/plane-2026-10/solution.json",
   "cwp:kind": "derive",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Model metres: x = E - 537550, z = -(N - 180300), y = m OD; WGS84 by the page's own quadratic fit (meta.geo) and its Newton inverse.",
    "Tower landmark = the apex (towers.json top.apex) or the centroid of the top tier at its top height; place landmark = area.js places at its ground height.",
    "Earth curvature is applied to every point (drop d^2/2R with refraction k = 0.13); the horizon target is the sea-level dip -sqrt(2h/R') with weight 0.5 (the visible horizon is hills 20 to 40 km away).",
    "Hold-out points are projected but not fitted; the run restarts once from its own result.",
    "The page view takes the fitted camera without k1 (the page has no lens distortion): eyeView(eye, heading, pitch, hfov) plus roll."
   ],
   "cwp:network": false,
   "cwp:deterministic": true,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuilddocklands"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuildtowers"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "sky",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "Pixel positions and which photo feature is which landmark are read by eye from grid enlargements; recorded in points.json and the photo folder's README (with the failed hold-out)."
  },
