   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/walk-portals.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/walk-portals.mjs <dgu|pdg|boroughs|nomis|onsgeo|national> walk [--refresh]; node cwplans/tools/walk-portals.mjs <portal> triage; NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/walk-portals.mjs <portal> harvest [key ...]; node cwplans/tools/walk-portals.mjs dgu catalogue; node cwplans/tools/walk-portals.mjs index",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Politeness: one request at a time over the run, at least 1.1 s apart, robots.txt read for every host before the first request and obeyed (longest matching rule), backoff on 429 and 5xx with Retry-After, the project User-Agent.",
    "Licence class (licenceClass in walk-portals.mjs): OGL, CC BY, ODC-By, CC0/PDDL/public domain are open; NC or closed is restricted; CC BY-SA and ODbL are share-alike (never harvested; OSM is the only share-alike exception); 'no conditions apply' alone is open-unclear; no licence is none (metadata only). data.gov.uk records with no licence whose resources all sit on GOV.UK, ONS, Nomis, NHS Digital, DfT road traffic or data.police.uk count as ogl-site-terms (those sites' terms give OGL v3.0).",
    "data.gov.uk scope: S1 local publishers (zone boroughs, LTGDC, Canal & River Trust, TfL, Royal Museums Greenwich, PLA, local NHS), S2 named national publishers, S3 the GLA (the London Datastore: state walked-elsewhere), S4 other publishers whose title or tags name a zone place or borough; out of scope only counted per organisation.",
    "data.gov.uk states, first match: T0 by hand; T1 sensitive title; T2 held (dataset id, or a name of 15+ characters with a hyphen, in a tool, data-register.json or pipeline.json); T3 walked-elsewhere (GLA); T4 unavailable (no resources); T5 not-relevant administrative (payments, spending, staff, contracts, FOI); T6 not-open; T7 not-relevant other area (bounding box misses the zone, or the title names another region, county, city or London borough); T8 deferred documents only; T9 listed-for-harvest (zone place, zone borough, London-fine or national-fine); T10 not-relevant coarser than a borough; T11 deferred area unknown.",
    "Zone place names (title and tags only, not the description): the London Datastore list plus Thames Barrier, Tideway, Lower Lea, Leamouth; not when the text has tree or crop words (Poplar is also a tree: 'Energy Crops Scheme' and short rotation coppice records matched it).",
    "planning.data.gov.uk: zone = entities whose geometry intersects the box polygon (the platform's spatial query); for documents, agreements and plans the entities of the zone planning organisations (GLA 144, Greenwich 150, Lewisham 198, City 203, Newham 246, Southwark 329, Tower Hamlets 350). States P0 by hand (held from another source), P1 harvested, P2 ended, P3 not-open, P4 empty, P5 code list, P6 nothing in the zone, P7 listed-for-harvest, P8 deferred.",
    "Harvest: whole geometries that meet the box are kept, rounded to 6 decimals, with in_zone, whole_in_zone, in_cw; EA flood zones are simplified (0.5 m) and cut at the box (clipped_to_zone). Fields matching e-mail, phone, contact, owner name, person, officer, agent, applicant are dropped and listed.",
    "Committed outputs stay small: the data.gov.uk triage lists datasets one by one only for the states that need a decision or hold data; the bulk states are name lists keyed by state, rule and reason. National files stay raw and uncommitted; only zone extracts are committed.",
    "Borough portals: City of London map service layers with the box envelope count; licence per layer from the City's data.gov.uk INSPIRE record (F42); layers about people or their sites deferred (B2); Southwark and Greenwich observatories read from the Esri UK InstantAtlas master tables and metadata service (indicators of national publishers are walked-elsewhere, B3); Lewisham licence from each JKAN source file; states B0-B8.",
    "Nomis: robots.txt disallows the API; the Census 2021 bulk zips are read, the OA CSV streamed, zone OAs (zone-codes.json oa21) kept; states N1-N3.",
    "ONS Open Geography: ArcGIS search catalogue; states G1-G8 by product family from the title; lookups read by code list in batches of 60.",
    "National: a hand-checked source list (licence, robots, state); STATS19 and police.uk kept as aggregates only (LSOA x year x severity; snap point x category, month x category), no record-level rows; STATS19 LSOA codes matched as 2011 and 2021 (F44); DESNZ workbooks read sheet by sheet, the header row is a short cell naming an LSOA/MSOA code."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "feeds",
   "cwp:fault": [
    "F42",
    "F43",
    "F44",
    "F45"
   ],
   "cwp:judgement": "The scope lists, the zone place exceptions, the JUDGED tables (held from another source, coarser than the zone) and the HARVEST tables were set by hand from the first triage; the reasons are in the tables and in feeds/portals/README.md. Licences that read 'no restrictions' without naming a licence (the Tower Hamlets ArcGIS Hub) are not treated as open."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolcachelondat",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "cache-londat",
   "dct:description": "Runs a subset of the existing fetch tools as child processes with their own politeness (fetch-live.mjs bikes lifts crowding ukpn overflows notams; fetch-river.mjs levels river-bus; fetch-ais.mjs --listen=0), asks two small endpoints itself (TfL line status by mode, Open-Meteo current weather; one request each), reads the snapshot JSON the tools wrote, replays this month's run files (cache/runs/) into a working SQLite (node:sqlite, WITHOUT ROWID tables with primary keys on the source's fetch or reading time), inserts the new snapshots and writes only the rows that were new as one small gzip JSON run file. The first run of a new month replays the previous month's run files into cache/live-YYYY-MM.sqlite (VACUUM) and removes them. Then writes cache/latest.json: per theme the newest fetch in compact columns and a 24 h series. --no-fetch appends from the snapshots already in the checkout. Planned to run hourly from a GitHub Actions workflow in danbri/londat (skill cwplans-londat-cache).",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/live/bikes.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/live/lifts.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/live/crowding.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/live/ukpn.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/live/overflows.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/live/notams.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/river/ais.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/river/levels.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/feeds/river/river-bus.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srctfllivefeeds",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.tfl.gov.uk/Line/Mode/tube,dlr,elizabeth-line,overground,river-bus,cable-car/Status",
     "dct:description": "one request per run"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcopenmeteo",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=51.505&longitude=-0.02&current=...",
     "dct:description": "one request per run"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/localdatarawcachethetworesponsesnofetchreadsthem"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/cache/runs/*/live-*.json.gz"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/cache/live-*.sqlite"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/cache/latest.json"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/cache-londat.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/cache-londat.mjs [--no-fetch] [--themes=bikes,lifts,...] [--vacuum]",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Idempotent: every table has a primary key with the fetch time of the snapshot (meta.fetched) or the reading time (tide, AIS positions, weather); INSERT OR IGNORE, so a second run on the same snapshots adds no rows.",
    "Politeness is the fetch tools' own (one request at a time per host, >= 1.5 s for TfL, >= 1 s for EA, >= 2 s and no stream for Open Waters); the tool adds two requests per run with up to two retries 3 and 6 s apart.",
    "Facts only, as the snapshots: no NOTAM text, no customer letter text from UK Power Networks, no JamCam images.",
    "Small private craft are never listed: the AIS filter of fetch-ais.mjs is repeated (ITU type 36/37, class B without a type are dropped) and their count is kept in ais_fetches.private_counted.",
    "Places (docks, stations, overflows, piers, gauges) are stored once in places and updated in place; state rows hold only ids and numbers.",
    "A run goes into the month of its newest snapshot; tide readings within 48 h of a month boundary can appear in two month files.",
    "Git size (coordinator, 2026-10-05): no binary file is committed per run; each run adds one run file (measured size in the skill) and latest.json; the monthly SQLite is committed once."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchlive"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchais"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "feeds",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "Which sources are cached (the live ones the pages show or ask for) and which are not: LAQN air quality (no open licence found), police.uk crime (monthly; the page asks on demand), JamCam images (TfL serves them), helicopter structure (static). Recorded in the skill cwplans-londat-cache."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchadsbcache",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "fetch-adsb-cache",
   "dct:description": "Streams the tar parts of each missing UTC day of the last 7 (a minimal tar reader; no file is written), gunzips each trace_full_<hex>.json, skips a trace with no latitude 51.x, parses it, and keeps the points within 25 nm of 51.505 N 0.02 W. Splits them into legs (the readsb new-leg flag, a gap of more than 10 minutes in the area, a change of callsign). Height: GNSS (alt_geom, ft above the WGS84 ellipsoid) when sent, else pressure altitude plus the hour's median (GNSS - pressure) of the area's aircraft below 10,000 ft; on the ground: flag. Writes one gzip JSON per UTC hour with the legs that overlap it (2 minutes before for trails, one point after), delta-coded integer columns [t s, lat and lon 1e-5 deg, alt 25 ft, height source, ground speed kt, track deg], a day.json with counts, index.json and a README with the ODbL notice; removes days older than 7. --push builds the orphan commit of the folder with a temporary index (GIT_INDEX_FILE, git write-tree, git commit-tree) and force-pushes it to refs/heads/adsb-cache, so the branch always has one commit.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcadsblol",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://github.com/adsblol/globe_history_<year>/releases/download/v<YYYY.MM.DD>-planes-readsb-prod-0/v<YYYY.MM.DD>-planes-readsb-prod-0.tar.aa (.ab, .ac, ...)",
     "dct:description": "one streamed download of each 2 GB part per new day (about 4.2 GB a day, nothing kept on disk); a HEAD request first to see whether the day's release exists"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/localbranchadsbcacheofdanbrilondatwithrestorethedaysalreadyheldbygitarchive"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "cwp:pathPattern": "branch adsb-cache: index.json, README.md, adsb/<YYYY-MM-DD>/day.json and adsb/<YYYY-MM-DD>/<HH>.json.gz (data-register.json 'branches')"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/fetch-adsb-cache.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node cwplans/tools/fetch-adsb-cache.mjs --out <dir> [--restore] [--push] [--days 7] [--date YYYY-MM-DD]",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Privacy rule of docklands/planes-live.js identified(): a callsign is kept only for an operator ICAO callsign (three letters and a digit) without the LADD or PIA flag (dbFlags 8, 4) and with an ICAO address (no '~'); every other leg gets an anonymous key (x<n>) and keeps only its type and category. No registration, owner (ownOp), squawk or ICAO address of an unidentified aircraft is written.",
    "Thinning: at most one point a second; above 15,000 ft at most one a minute (the 3D page shows high traffic as context only).",
    "Not on main: the cache is on the orphan branch adsb-cache with one commit, so git history does not grow each day; the main working tree and index are never touched.",
    "Licence: ODbL 1.0 (owner approval 2026-10-09 for the committed cache); the branch README and every page view carry 'Aircraft: © adsb.lol contributors, ODbL'.",
    "Politeness: one download at a time, User-Agent naming this repository; a day whose release is not yet published is skipped and fetched by the next run."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": true,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "sky",
   "cwp:fault": []
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolfetchlivecache",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "fetch-live-cache",
   "dct:description": "Asks the three sources once each and adds the answers to rolling buffers. Aircraft: each report [t = answer time - seen_pos, lat, lon, altitude above the WGS84 ellipsoid (alt_geom, else alt_baro + the answer's median (alt_geom - alt_baro) below 10,000 ft), height source, ground speed, track, vertical rate, turn rate], the last 60 minutes. Ships: the newest position of each kept vessel added when it moved or 30 minutes passed; positions of the last 2 hours, the newest kept at any age while Open Waters lists the vessel. METAR: the reports of the last 24 hours with visibility in metres from the report text. A source that fails keeps its previous file. --push builds the orphan commit with a temporary index (GIT_INDEX_FILE, git write-tree, git commit-tree) and force-pushes refs/heads/live-cache, so the branch always has one commit.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcadsblol",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://api.adsb.lol/v2/point/51.505/-0.02/25",
     "dct:description": "one GET a run (every 5 minutes), User-Agent naming this repository; 3 tries on 429, 5xx and timeouts"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcopenwatersais",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://ais.openwaters.io/v1/vessels?bbox=51.474,-0.095,51.528,0.085",
     "dct:description": "one GET a run, anonymous tier"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcawcmetar",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://aviationweather.gov/api/data/metar?ids=EGLC&format=json&hours=24",
     "dct:description": "one GET a run"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/localbranchlivecacheofdanbrilondatwithrestorethepreviousaircraftjsonshipsjsonandmetarjsonbygitfetchdepth1andgitshow"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/localbranchlivecachereadmemdaircraftjsonshipsjsonmetarjsondataregisterjsonbranches"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/fetch-live-cache.mjs"
   },
