   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toollondonterrain",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "london-terrain",
   "dct:description": "Makes a 250 m lattice in British National Grid (E 503000-562000, N 155000-201000, 237 x 185 points), turns each point to WGS84 (OSGB36 Helmert, about 2 m out) and asks the OpenTopoData public API for EU-DEM v1.1 heights, 100 points a request at most one request a second, with a User-Agent. Points already in the raw file are not asked again (the raw file is the cache; saved every 10 requests). The operation fills no-data points with the mean of their known neighbours and writes the heights in decimetres in the page frame (x = E - 537550, z = -(N - 180300)), north to south as A.terrain. The page (terrain-ring.js) draws the grid outside the model box and joins it to the LiDAR ground at the box edge.",
