  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuildroofs",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "build-roofs",
   "dct:description": "tools/lidar-roofs.py mosaics the DSM and DTM tiles (read from the zips), takes for each model building of 25 m or less (no holes, no min_height) the 1 m cells whose centres are inside the outline and 0.75 m or more from its edges, subtracts the model ground, and fits four roofs by least squares with one trimming pass, in the outline's minimum-area rectangle: flat; gable with the ridge along the long side and along the short side (ridge offset searched in 0.5 m steps within 30 % of the span); hipped (equal pitch on four sides). build-roofs.mjs keeps a pitched fit when its slope is 0.18 to 1.8, its rise 1 m or more, its eave 2 m or more, its median absolute error 0.45 m or less and at most 0.7 of the flat fit's and a quarter of the rise; a hipped fit only when its error is under 0.8 of the best gable's (pyramidal when the rectangle's sides are within 1.2 of each other). Else flat (error 0.3 m or less) or complex. Where the LiDAR gives no shape, OSM roof:shape gabled, hipped or pyramidal is used (ridge at the model height, roof:height, roof:levels x 2.5 m or a 35 deg pitch), unless the LiDAR fit in that ridge direction slopes the wrong way. Writes the page file and, per building with a shape, its shape, eave, ridge, ridge bearing and basis to the graph. Since operation version 2 (2026-10-08): a fifth fit, one inclined plane (skillion, slope 0.08 to 1.0, kept when its error is under 0.8 of the best gable's); an outline that is not a rectangle (area under 0.9 of its minimum-area rectangle) is cut into parts with chords from its reflex corners along a long edge (3 m or more, within 12 deg), the cut chosen by the least waste against the parts' rectangles and, between equal cuts, by the LiDAR error; each part is fitted as a building, with cells 0.4 m or more from the cuts. A complex building with one pitched part, or a pitched building whose parts' summed error is under 0.75 of its one roof's, is drawn in parts (flat parts at their fitted level, at least 2 m); a gable that ends at a cut against a crossing wing (ridges 53 to 127 deg apart, its ridge at most 0.3 m above the other's) runs on to that wing's ridge, so the page draws a valley. The pieces are cut with roofs-layer.js pieces() and checked against the rings of lidar-roofs.py.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/area.js"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/building-keys.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/lidar-roofs.py"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/roofs-layer.js"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcealidar",
     "dct:description": "EA survey tiles TQ3075, TQ3080, TQ3575, TQ3580: lidar_composite_first_return_dsm/2022/1 and lidar_composite_dtm/2022/1 (https://environment.data.gov.uk/tiles/collections/survey/<product>/2022/1/<tile>, fetched 2026-10-08; not committed, 60 to 72 MB each; SHA-256 in the activity log)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/localdatarawdocklandsgreaterlondonlatestosmpbf"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srcosm"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/docklands/data/roofs.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/srckgx"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/londat/blob/main/cwplans/tools/build-roofs.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "ROOFS_TILES=<dir of the 8 tile zips> ROOFS_PBF=<greater_london-latest.osm.pbf> node cwplans/tools/build-roofs.mjs",
   "cwp:kind": "build",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Towers (over 25 m) keep their flat tops (data/towers.json models the tall ones); outlines with holes or a min_height stay prisms.",
    "The page draws a roof only while roofs.json's model fingerprint matches the page (MFP); rerun after build-docklands.mjs and key-model-buildings.mjs.",
    "ROOFS_DRY=1 with ROOFS_MEAS=<lidar-roofs.py output> writes the page file without a log entry while the rules are tuned; the committed file comes from a logged run."
   ],
   "cwp:network": false,
   "cwp:deterministic": true,
   "cwp:after": [
