  {
   "@id": "https://kgx.foaf.tv/id/toolbuildmaterials",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "build-materials",
   "dct:description": "For each model building: the OSM element (building-keys.json; a part also reads its parent) gives the building type, levels and, from the extract (osmium tags-filter), building:material, building:colour, roof:material, roof:colour, shop and amenity. OSM shop and amenity nodes (shops, cafes, restaurants, pubs, bars, banks, pharmacies and similar) are projected to the model through OSTN15 and matched to the outline that holds them, else to the nearest outline edge within 2.5 m. A facade style follows from the type, height, footprint area and registry use (rules R); the wall material is the OSM tag when there is one, else a weighted pick by style, seeded by a hash of the OSM id so that neighbours differ; an OSM colour replaces the material colour (glass: mixed with it). The storey class is the nearest of four storey heights of the style to the wall height (to the eave of a roofs.json roof) over the OSM levels, else a hashed spread round the default. Pitched and flat roof colours come from roof:material and roof:colour, else weighted picks. The guessed Night use (homes, offices) is only used where the registry gives none.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
